      "instruction": "You will hear two students planning a research project. Complete questions one to six. Write no more than two words and or a number for each answer. Listen for what they finally agree. You now have thirty seconds to read the questions.",
      "voices": {
        "Mia": "Katie",
        "Leo": "James"
      },
      "turns": [
        [
          "Mia",
          "Let's keep our voices down a little. This is the quiet study area. Did you look at the tutor's comments on our project proposal?"
        ],
        [
          "Leo",
          "Yes. Our first idea, public transport, was too broad. I think food waste would be easier to investigate locally."
        ],
        [
          "Mia",
          "Agreed. Food waste it is. We can find out what happens to unsold food. Were you still thinking of using a questionnaire?"
        ],
        [
          "Leo",
          "I was, but the tutor wants us to explore people's reasons, not just count responses. Let's use interviews instead. We can ask follow-up questions when an answer isn't clear."
        ],
        [
          "Mia",
          "That makes sense. At first I thought we could talk to customers, but they probably wouldn't know how much gets thrown away."
        ],
        [
          "Leo",
          "Exactly. Shop owners can explain that, so they should be our participants. We can ask how they plan their orders and deal with anything left over."
        ],
        [
          "Mia",
          "How many interviews do we need? I wrote fifteen in our first draft."
        ],
        [
          "Leo",
          "The tutor said we must complete at least twelve. Fifteen would be useful, but twelve is the minimum we need to plan for."
        ],
        [
          "Mia",
          "Fine. Let's divide the work evenly. Could we meet on Wednesday to check the interview questions before we contact anyone?"
        ],
        [
          "Leo",
          "I have a laboratory session then. Thursday works for me, and it still gives us enough time."
        ],
        [
          "Mia",
          "Thursday is good. Shall we meet back here in the library?"
        ],
        [
          "Leo",
          "We need to practise asking the questions aloud, so this quiet area won't work. I've booked Room Four in the study centre. Let's meet there."
        ],
        [
          "Mia",
          "Great. I'll bring the draft questions. Before we leave, let's check that none of them tells people what answer we expect."
        ],
        [
          "Leo",
          "Good idea. We want to hear their experience, even if it doesn't match what we predicted."
        ]
